IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-bigamy`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-bigamy.l4 (sections 56 and
-- 57).  Every expected value was decided from the section's text before the assertion
-- was written, and is stated beside it.

§ `Tests: child-stealing and bigamy`

§§ `Section 56`

#ASSERT `s 56: only the title survives in this text` EQUALS "Section 56 keeps its title, Child-stealing, but its text is a row of dots; nothing is encoded."

§§ `Section 57`

-- was married, married another person, the former husband or wife was then living, the
-- second marriage took place in England or Ireland, the person is a subject of Her
-- Majesty, complete years of continual absence, knew the spouse to be living within that
-- time, had been divorced, former marriage had been declared void
`s57 the plain case` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 second marriage elsewhere, by a subject` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 second marriage elsewhere, by a non-subject` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 second marriage in England, by a non-subject` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 spouse absent 7 years, not known to be living` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 7, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 spouse absent 6 years, not known to be living` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 6, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 spouse absent 10 years, not known to be living` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 10, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 spouse absent 7 years but known to be living` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 7, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 divorced from the first marriage` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s57 former marriage declared void` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s57 not married` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 did not marry another person` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s57 the former husband or wife was not living` MEANS `Conduct under section 57` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 57: bigamy` `s57 the plain case`
-- "whether the second marriage shall have taken place in England or Ireland or elsewhere"
#ASSERT `s 57: bigamy` `s57 second marriage elsewhere, by a subject`
-- exception (1) needs BOTH elsewhere AND not a subject
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 second marriage elsewhere, by a non-subject`)
#ASSERT `s 57: bigamy` `s57 second marriage in England, by a non-subject`
-- exception (2): seven years is the boundary; six is not enough, seven is, ten is
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 spouse absent 7 years, not known to be living`)
#ASSERT `s 57: bigamy` `s57 spouse absent 6 years, not known to be living`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 spouse absent 10 years, not known to be living`)
-- ... and it fails if the spouse was known to be living within that time
#ASSERT `s 57: bigamy` `s57 spouse absent 7 years but known to be living`
-- exceptions (3) and (4)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 divorced from the first marriage`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 former marriage declared void`)
-- elements missing
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 not married`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 did not marry another person`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: bigamy` `s57 the former husband or wife was not living`)
#ASSERT `s 57: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
-- seven years = 84 months
#ASSERT `s 57: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` (`for a term not exceeding` 84)
-- each exception on its own, as a rule
#ASSERT `s 57: exception for a spouse continually absent seven years and not known to be living` `s57 spouse absent 7 years, not known to be living`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57: exception for a spouse continually absent seven years and not known to be living` `s57 spouse absent 6 years, not known to be living`)
#ASSERT `s 57: exception for a second marriage contracted abroad by a person who is not a subject` `s57 second marriage elsewhere, by a non-subject`
#ASSERT `s 57: exception for a person divorced from the first marriage` `s57 divorced from the first marriage`
#ASSERT `s 57: exception for a former marriage declared void` `s57 former marriage declared void`
